// Madness = two abilities on one keyword ([CR#702.35a]): a self-replacement
// that EXILES the card instead of discarding it to the graveyard, and a
// (reflexive-unified delayed) triggered ability that lets its owner cast it for
// the madness cost when it is exiled this way — else it goes to the graveyard.
//
// Usage: on a card, `Keyword(Madness([Mana([Generic(1),Red])]))` = "Madness
// {1}{R}". Template: "madness ${0}".
//
// The param is a `Cost` (the madness cost list). It appears in ONE slot: the
// delayed trigger's `Cast(EventObject, <cost>)` alternative-cost facet, so the
// exiled card is cast paying the madness cost RATHER THAN its mana cost
// ([CR#118.9,702.35a]).
//
// Shape, and why each piece is where it is:
//
//   Static(Replacement(Instead(would: Discard(Any, Ref(This)), instead: …)))
//     — the self-replacement. It functions from the HAND (madness's card is in
//     hand when discarded); the engine gathers it as a self-replacement on the
//     affected object even off the battlefield. The `would` is the bare-verb
//     `Discard(who, what)` twin narrowed to THIS card. An `Instead` replaces the
//     discard intent away entirely, so a SECOND madness (Falkenrath Gorger's
//     granted "choose one") can never also fire on the same discard — exactly
//     one Instead applies per intent ([CR#616.1]), the stacked-madness "applies
//     once" outcome with ZERO semantic guard clause.
//
//     The discard NAME-fact still stands: the keyword-action discard window's
//     `FinalizeAct` watches THIS card and commits its `Act(Discard)` name-fact
//     on ANY zone change of the card since the window opened, destination-
//     agnostic — so the exile below still finalizes a discard and Megrim /
//     "whenever you discard" fires ([CR#701.9c,702.35a] "that player discards
//     it, but…"), even though the content committed to Exile, not the graveyard.
//
//   With(binder: Produce(Move(This, Exile, [], Hand)), body: Delayed(…))
//     — `Produce` performs the Hand → Exile move and binds the exiled card as
//     `That` (chased through the remint, [CR#400.7j]) — the lexical "…this way"
//     linkage. The move's `from: Hand` guard fizzles the whole thing if the
//     card already left the hand ([CR#701.9a]).
//
//   Delayed(event: ZoneChange(what: Ref(This), from: Hand, to: Exile), effect: May(…))
//     — a REAL triggered ability ([CR#702.35a] — it uses the stack, priority,
//     is stiflable). Installed AFTER the exile it watches, it is reflexive-
//     unified ([CR#603.7,603.12]): it fires on that just-produced exile rather
//     than waiting for a future one. `This` in its event/anchor is the produced
//     card (the source moved itself away, so the created-trigger context falls
//     back to the `That` product). The fired body reads the exiled card as
//     `EventObject`.
//
//   May(who: You, effect: Cast(You, EventObject, Param(0)), if_not: Move(EventObject, Graveyard, [], Exile))
//     — the owner may cast the exiled card for the madness cost (`Cast`'s
//     alternative-cost slot, [CR#118.9]); the "yes" offer is gated on a legal,
//     payable cast ([CR#608.2g]). If they don't, it moves Exile → graveyard —
//     an ORDINARY future move, so Rest in Peace / Leyline of the Void bite it
//     normally (the madness+RiP ruling falls out for free).
(
    name: "Madness",
    template: "madness ${0}",
    kinds: [KeywordAbility],
    params: [Cost],
    body: Composite(
        name: "Madness",
        abilities: [Static(Replacement(Instead(
            would: Discard(Any, Ref(This)),
            instead: With(
                binder: Produce(Move(This, Exile, [], Hand)),
                body: Delayed(
                    event: ZoneChange(what: Ref(This), from: Hand, to: Exile),
                    effect: May(
                        who: You,
                        effect: Cast(You, EventObject, Param(0)),
                        if_not: Move(EventObject, Graveyard, [], Exile),
                    ),
                ),
            ),
        )))],
    ),
)
